Rollback compatibility with the redesigned patch set. Delete it once rolling
back from that patch set to this release is no longer supported.

The redesigned patch set gives Ray worker groups no minCount, while this
release sets every worker group's minCount to its minReplicas and compares
minCount when it checks that a job still matches its Workload. After a
rollback, every running RayCluster, RayJob, and RayService the redesign
admitted would stop matching, and Kueue would delete its Workload and suspend
it. The Ray integrations now ignore minCount in that check while the Workload
holds quota.

The redesign also adds the PartialPreemption feature gate, which Kueue
refuses as unknown at startup, so this release defines it and ignores it;
and it registers the RayCluster defaulting webhook for UPDATE, where this
release's create-time defaults could suspend a running RayCluster, so the
webhook now leaves updates unchanged.

